Package: libqe
Title: Shared C++ Core for Quantitative Ethnography Packages
Type: Package
Author: Cody L Marquart [aut, cre]
Authors@R: c(person("Cody L", "Marquart", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "cody.marquart@wisc.edu", comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-3387-6792")))
Maintainer: Cody L Marquart <cody.marquart@wisc.edu>
Version: 0.1.0
Description: Header-only C++ library providing shared computational primitives for
    quantitative ethnography packages (rENA, tma, and others). Exposes four modules
    via inst/include/libqe/: adjacency vector utilities, normalization, ENA modeling
    and node positioning, and stanza/tensor-based accumulation. R packages consume
    this via LinkingTo; Python packages consume it via pybind11. This package also
    exports Rcpp-wrapped versions of every function for direct testing and use in R.
License: GPL-3
URL: https://gitlab.com/epistemic-analytics/qe-packages/libqe
BugReports: https://gitlab.com/epistemic-analytics/qe-packages/libqe/-/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
LinkingTo: Rcpp, RcppArmadillo
Imports:
    Rcpp
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 2.1.0),
    rENA,
    tma
RoxygenNote: 7.3.3
NeedsCompilation: yes
